de":"LEFT","line":119,"original_line":119,"side":"LEFT","in_reply_to_id":3525341468,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":27,"position":27,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3628954053","pull_request_review_id":4752798375,"id":3628954053,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc7YTXHF","diff_hunk":"@@ -107,16 +108,14 @@ uint encode_norm_to_uint_oct(vec3 base) {\n \n uint encode_tang_to_uint_oct(vec4 base) {\n \tvec2 oct = vec3_to_oct(base.xyz);\n+\n+\t// 0.5 cannot be represented in UNORM16\n+\toct.y = clamp(oct.y, 1.0 / 65535.0, 65534.0 / 65535.0);\n+\n \t// Encode binormal sign in y component\n \toct.y = oct.y * 0.5f + 0.5f;\n \toct.y = base.w >= 0.0f ? oct.y : 1 - oct.y;\n \n-\tif (oct.x == 0.0 && oct.y == 1.0) {\n-\t\t// (1, 1) and (0, 1) decode to the same value, but (0, 1) messes with our compression detection.\n-\t\t// So we sanitize here.\n-\t\toct.x = 1.0;\n-\t}\n-","path":"servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/skeleton.glsl","commit_id":"5ae06178f2da85f5a4d28d3420737ffb872e6a23","original_commit_id":"a5ca958b4d2fcd9e4e28922a74e9cebba4dbb508","user":{"login":"Gaktan","id":1674095,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzQwOTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1674095?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaktan","html_url":"https://github.com/Gaktan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaktan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaktan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaktan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaktan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaktan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaktan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaktan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaktan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gaktan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I did a test in python to validate my assumptions. Interestingly, I don't get the same result as from the paper, I believe this is because I am comparing directions against a 64bits vector reference, whereas the paper compares against 32 bits as the reference.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1876\" height=\"866\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2aae53db-db80-4bae-856d-b61f6cc08cae\" />\r\n\r\nHow to read this graph:\r\nI am generating 1 million unit vector directions using a Fibonacci distribution for better uniformity. This direction is encoded in a Vector3 with 64bits per channel. From this reference vector, I compute a Vector3 with 32bits per channel (float32). From this 32 bit vector, I compute the octahedral encoding, quantize it in 16bits per channel (Oct32), then decode it to a Vector3 again to measure the angle error from the encoding/quantization/decoding.\r\nI do the same thing again, but clamping the quantized result before decoding (Oct32_clamped).\r\n\r\nAll the graphs here represent the error compared to the reference 64 bits Vector, measured in degrees.\r\n\r\n* Top left is a histogram representing the distribution of the error angle\r\n* Top right is a box plot of the same data, showing mean value and standard deviation\r\n* Finally a table that shows precise values\r\n\r\nAs you can see, there is no difference between the clamped/unclamped encoding, suggesting that the error between the two is minimal.\r\n\r\nIn good faith, I also tried with Oct30 (15 bits per channel, since Godot uses 1 bit for the binormal sign), and I get similar results.\r\n\r\nI also did another test, which is actually closer to what is happening with my proposed fix, by using the Oct32 decoded result as a reference:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1876\" height=\"866\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8c339da4-5d22-4347-8e20-908725fec1d0\" />\r\n\r\nYou can see the max error is negligible with 0.0442 degrees. Again, we are talking about a TANGENT vector, so the error is far less important than the normal error.\r\n\r\nI can provided the code for my test if needed.","created_at":"2026-07-22T09:06:31Z","updated_at":"2026-07-22T09:06:32Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120901#discussion_r3628954053","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120901","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3628954053"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120901#discussion_r3628954053"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120901"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3628954053/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":114,"original_start_line":114,"start_side":"LEFT","line":119,"original_line":119,"side":"LEFT","in_reply_to_id":3525341468,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":27,"position":27,"subject_type":"line"}]